Subject: [PATCH] armv8-m: preserve SysTick time across counter boundaries

Base: apache/nuttx 2b5c0de5e933281c209f954a63b99cf10c132346 (13.1.0)

SysTick continues counting while its interrupt is masked. Sampling CURRENT
before the pending bit can combine a pre-wrap count with a post-wrap pending
interrupt, making CLOCK_MONOTONIC regress after the ISR advances the timebase.
Take a stable pending/current snapshot before converting the counter.

Keep the raw count for the zero tests: a positive sub-microsecond count rounds
to zero microseconds but is near expiry, not a newly reset counter. Correct
both pending and nonpending elapsed-time calculations without clamping time.
The existing single-pending-bit limitation after multiple masked wraps remains.

The native regression extracts the original and patched functions and injects
MMIO transitions. The original fails the three wrap/rounding cases; the patch
preserves all five normal/reset/callback controls. Fresh MPS2 QEMU runs exercise
the clock through actual blocked std channel transfers. This is a correctness
fix, not evidence of physical timing or a performance improvement.

diff --git a/arch/arm/src/armv8-m/arm_systick.c b/arch/arm/src/armv8-m/arm_systick.c
--- a/arch/arm/src/armv8-m/arm_systick.c
+++ b/arch/arm/src/armv8-m/arm_systick.c
@@ -155,19 +155,32 @@
 {
   struct systick_lowerhalf_s *lower = (struct systick_lowerhalf_s *)lower_;
   irqstate_t flags = up_irq_save();
+  uint32_t current;
+  bool pending;
 
   status->flags    = lower->callback ? TCFLAGS_HANDLER : 0;
   status->flags   |= systick_is_running() ? TCFLAGS_ACTIVE : 0;
   status->timeout  = usec_from_count(
     RELOAD2TIMEOUT(getreg32(NVIC_SYSTICK_RELOAD)), lower->freq);
-  status->timeleft = usec_from_count(getreg32(NVIC_SYSTICK_CURRENT),
-                                     lower->freq);
+  /* The counter keeps running while interrupts are masked.  If it wraps
+   * between sampling CURRENT and the pending bit, a pre-wrap count must not
+   * be combined with a post-wrap pending interrupt.  Retry that transition.
+   */
 
-  if (systick_irq_pending(lower))
+  do
+    {
+      pending = systick_irq_pending(lower);
+      current = getreg32(NVIC_SYSTICK_CURRENT);
+    }
+  while (pending != systick_irq_pending(lower));
+
+  status->timeleft = usec_from_count(current, lower->freq);
+
+  if (pending)
     {
       /* Interrupt is pending and the timer wrap happen? */
 
-      if (status->timeleft)
+      if (current != 0)
         {
           /* Make timeout-timeleft equal the real elapsed time */
 
@@ -175,8 +188,12 @@
           status->timeleft = 0;
         }
     }
-  else if (status->timeleft == 0)
+  else if (current == 0)
     {
+      /* Only raw zero denotes a reset counter.  A nonzero sub-microsecond
+       * count also rounds to zero, but is near the end of the interval.
+       */
+
       status->timeleft = status->timeout;
     }
 
